+| `sessions[].createdAt`  | string | ISO-8601 creation time                    |
+| `sessions[].updatedAt`  | string | ISO-8601 last-activity time               |
+| `sessions[].entryCount` | number | Number of entries in the conversation     |
+
+A store without `listFor` answers an empty `session_list`; a failing `listFor` produces `SERVER_ERROR` and is logged without closing the socket. ([validated by: answers an empty session_list when the store has no listFor, and SERVER_ERROR with a ws error log when listFor throws](../../src/transport/conversationList.acceptance.test.ts#L113))
+
 ## 6. SessionEntry Objects

 A SessionEntry represents a single piece of content in the conversation. Every entry has a `role` field that determines its shape. The `role` acts as a discriminant for the union type.
